@using EliteIndustries.Models
@*
    Homepage hero band.

    One image and nothing over it: the client's "Solution for export packaging"
    infographic. Its labels are part of the artwork, so the alt text carries
    them for assistive tech and crawlers. The page's only <h1> sits here,
    visually hidden — the artwork already says what the page is about, and a
    visible heading on top of it would repeat its own title.

    The image is the LCP element: not lazy, fetchpriority="high", and with its
    intrinsic width/height so the band reserves its height before it arrives.
    It is never cropped — see wwwroot/css/hero.css.
*@

<section class="ei-hero" aria-labelledby="ei-hero-title">
    <h1 class="ei-sr" id="ei-hero-title">@CompanyProfile.Name — @CompanyProfile.Tagline</h1>

    <div class="ei-hero-frame">
        <img class="ei-hero-img"
             src="~/img/hero-export-packaging.jpeg"
             asp-append-version="true"
             width="1280"
             height="596"
             fetchpriority="high"
             alt="Solution for export packaging: an open truck loaded with pallets of cargo, surrounded by the eight products used to pack and secure it — PP collapsible boxes, PET strap, paper angle board, PP separator sheet, stretch film, composite strap, air dunnage bag and ratchet belt." />
    </div>
</section>
